            <ArticleTitle>Myocardial infarction caused by a large coronary artery aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1568-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A large coronary aneurysm, originating from a side branch of the right coronary artery, caused recurrent ischemia resulting in myocardial infarction. Successful surgical excision, without concomitant coronary artery bypass grafting, is described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
